    "result_text": "All 34 tests pass, including the membership-level tests (Cp15, Cp21, Cp23, Cp24) and the surrounding suite.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133, computed at creation):\n\n- **`model/MembershipLevels.java`** (new) \u2014 shared helper implementing the rule: start at 1, +1 for a present email, +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure).\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 response mapping now targets `membershipLevel` via the helper; the old GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE `membershipTier` expression is gone.\n- **`function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel=\u2026` instead of nothing tier-related, satisfying Cp21 (the audit line carries the level alongside the id).\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 the schema field became `membershipLevel` (integer, 1\u20133, read-only), so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes `membershipLevel` and no longer has `membershipTier`.\n\n`householdSize` was left untouched since the new rule doesn't use it and it's a separate persisted attribute. The former GOLD-tier behaviour is intentionally dropped, as Cp23 confirms (a 3-member household now yields level 2, not a tier).",
